{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumspanningtree(weight:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumSpanningTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/SpanningForest","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV","text":"SpanningForest"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP","text":"AdditiveArithmetic"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","text":"Comparable"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Edges are ordered by weight, then by position in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"text":". Under that order the minimum","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spanning forest is unique, and this is it. Its edges are listed in nondecreasing weight","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and, among equal weights, in position order, and the weight is added up in that order.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Sparse graphs (fewer than 4 edges per vertex) run Kruskal’s algorithm; denser ones run","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Prim’s under the same order and sort the edges taken.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives each edge’s weight from its position, so parallel edges can differ. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"called once for each edge that is not a self-loop and is not kept. Negative, zero and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"infinite weights are ordinary weights. A NaN weight traps; filter such edges out first.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(m log m).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Complexity","type":"aside","style":"note"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No weight is NaN; the sum of the chosen weights, in the order listed, does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not overflow and is not NaN.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Precondition","type":"aside","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumSpanningTree(weight:)"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum spanning forest: o